@startuml
title UC9 - PvP Battle - Use Case Description

map "UC9 - PvP Battle" as UC9 {
  Name => PvP Battle
  ID => UC9
  Description => Two players engage in real-time turn-based Pokemon battle over network
  Actor => Player, PvP Server
  Organizational Benefits => Competitive multiplayer experience and end-game content
  Trigger => Matchmaking (UC8) successfully pairs two players
  Preconditions => 1. Both players matched via UC8 (Matchmaking) \n 2. BattleRoom created on PvP Server \n 3. Both players connected via SignalR (BattleHub)
  Postconditions => 1. Battle result recorded \n 2. PvP stats updated in MySQL database
  Main Course => 1. Server initializes BattleRoom with both players teams \n 2. System displays opponent active Pokemon and battle UI \n 3. Both players select their action simultaneously \n 4. Server collects both actions via PvPManager \n 5. Server determines turn order based on Speed stats \n 6. Server executes actions sequentially (faster first) \n 7. Server broadcasts battle state to both clients \n 8. Repeat steps 3-7 until one side has no Pokemon \n 9. Server declares winner, updates PvPWins/PvPLosses \n 10. System saves results and returns to Main Menu
  Alternate Courses => 1. Player selects Switch -> swap active Pokemon \n 2. Player selects Items -> use item \n 3. Player Pokemon faints -> forced switch \n 4. Player forfeits -> opponent wins by default
  Exceptions => 1. Opponent disconnects -> Player wins by default \n 2. Network timeout -> attempt reconnection, forfeit after timeout \n 3. Server crash -> battle voided, no stats changed
}

@enduml
